    "created_at": "2025-06-19T10:11:53Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-06-19T10:11:53Z",
    "body": "> However, can you help reassure me that everything has web platform tests?\r\n\r\nThe tests have somewhat organically grown due to the lack of specification around this, and in addition a lot of this is \"action at a distance\", so they're not neatly organised but:\r\n\r\n- https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/html/semantics/interactive-elements/the-dialog-element/dialog-showModal-remove.html this tests that a dialog in the modal state can be removed.\r\n- https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/html/semantics/interactive-elements/the-dialog-element/dialog-remove-open-attr-crash.html this tests that a dialog in the modal state doesn't crash when the `open` attribute is removed (the current spec would hit this)\r\n- https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/html/semantics/interactive-elements/the-dialog-element/dialog-requestclose-2-crash.html, https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/html/semantics/interactive-elements/the-dialog-element/dialog-requestclose-3-crash.html,https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/html/semantics/interactive-elements/the-dialog-element/dialog-requestclose-4-crash.html, https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/html/semantics/interactive-elements/the-dialog-element/dialog-requestclose-crash.html all test the various combinations of attribute/insertions while calling `requestClose` which - due to its close watcher integration - hits various asserts around the state of the internal close watcher.\r\n\r\nWe could probably improve coverage, or at least organise it so it is more explicitly aligned to these spec changes, but overall I feel confident with the tests in place, but happy to take suggestions or guidance if you feel it's insufficient.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
